<mujoco model="pc_fumehood_push">
  <!-- Non-prehensile push suite in the PAPER fume hood.

       The frozen paper shell (room walls + ceiling, bench, hood sides/back/top,
       frame posts, mocap sash and jambs, legacy parked bodies, outside pedestal
       and tray) is included verbatim through pact_place_corridor_v5.xml and is
       never edited. This file only ADDS:

         * a pool of real lab items built from primitives (bottles, flask,
           beaker, tube rack, glove box, stirrer hotplate, carboy, ring stand,
           sharps bin, tip box, graduated cylinder). Every item is a mocap body
           whose frame origin is the centre of its BASE, so the sampler poses
           it at (x, y, bench_top_z) and it rests exactly on the work surface.
           Unused items are parked under the floor. Names are pact_clutter_*
           so contact scoring classifies them as clutter hazards.
         * a flat goal decal (tape ring on the work surface). Contactless
           (contype=0, conaffinity=0), 1.2 mm thick, visible to the cameras.

       The pushed container itself (cavity_obj_0/push_jar) is added by the
       task sampler at compile time (pc_fumehood_push.py). -->
